        <title type="html"><![CDATA[CSSStyleDeclaration.setProperty() find stylesheet by name not index]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41380</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41380"/>
        <updated>2025-10-03T05:08:02.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #41379.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3479515543" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41379" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/41379/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41379">#41379</a></p>
<p dir="auto">The interesting bit of this is that it finds the stylesheet to use based on the name of the generated output inline style block, which I discovered by inspection. Provided this does not change it is more robust for examples. More important though, it is a better technique for finding a style of interest.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="const stylesheet = document.styleSheets[1];
// Find the inline stylesheet generated for MDN live samples
const stylesheet = document.querySelector(&quot;style#css-output&quot;).sheet;"><pre class="notranslate"><span class="pl-k">const</span> <span class="pl-s1">stylesheet</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-smi">document</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-c1">styleSheets</span><span class="pl-kos">[</span><span class="pl-c1">1</span><span class="pl-kos">]</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-c">// Find the inline stylesheet generated for MDN live samples</span>
<span class="pl-k">const</span> <span class="pl-s1">stylesheet</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-smi">document</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">querySelector</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">"style#css-output"</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-c1">sheet</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">FYI is also possible to search for external stylesheets. We need to document that somewhere too. Something like this.</p>
<div class="snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="// Find the stylesheet by its href
const stylesheet = [...document.styleSheets].find(
  (s) =&gt; s.href?.includes(&quot;your-styles.css&quot;)
);"><pre class="notranslate"><code class="notranslate">// Find the stylesheet by its href
const stylesheet = [...document.styleSheets].find(
  (s) =&gt; s.href?.includes("your-styles.css")
);
</code></pre></div>]]></content>
